title: 'pallet-revive: fix v4 migration for runtimes that enabled PGasDeposit before it'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes `pallet_revive::migrations::v4` on runtimes that switched `Config::Deposit` to
    `PGasDeposit` before scheduling v4.

    After v4, every account holding a deposit holds exactly the native recorded in its
    `NativeDepositOf` rows. Native with no row was paid before the switch: it is burned and the
    same amount of PGAS is minted and held under the same reason. When that storage is freed, the
    payer gets `RefundPercent` of it back in PGAS and the rest is burned. Native paid after the
    switch keeps its row and is still refunded in native. Each reconciled account is given the
    PGAS existential deposit, frozen, as a new contract is.

    Code deposit rows are rebuilt from `CodeInfoOf` only when the pallet account has no rows and no
    PGAS on hold, i.e. every code deposit was paid in native.

    Fixed:
    - Code deposits were credited twice when rows already existed.
    - Contracts' recorded native was swapped, so those payers' refunds failed with
      `StorageRefundLocked`.
    - A failed swap burned native without minting PGAS. It now rolls back and is logged.
    - Delegated accounts' deposits were not migrated.
    - `DeletionQueue` entries already in the new layout were overwritten with a zero account.
    - Each step iteration now does one item of work (a code entry, an account, a row,
      a swap or a queue slot) at its own benchmarked weight.

    The pallet now refuses calls, instantiations, code upload and removal, and `set_code` with
    `Error::MigrationsOngoing` while a multi-block migration runs. This covers XCM and scheduled
    calls, which the executive does not pause. Dry runs are still served.

    Runtimes that have not run v4 yet:
    - Register the PGAS asset before scheduling v4, and run the `try-runtime` checks. A swap that
      fails on chain is skipped, not retried.
    - Expect XCM that calls into revive to fail while migrations run, unless the runtime pauses
      `MessageQueue` for that time.
    - `migrations::v4::Cursor` is now generic (use `CursorOf<T>`) and has new variants.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
